.TH TOP 1
.UC
.SH NAME
top \- display active processes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B top
[
.B \-d
.I seconds
]
[
.B \-l
.I lines
]
[
.B \-n
.I count
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Top
prints a small process table sorted by the kernel scheduler CPU usage
counter.
It also prints load average and a compact memory summary.
The memory summary reports the live user process image, including swapped
processes.
.PP
The
.B \-d
option sets the refresh delay.
The
.B \-l
option sets the number of process rows.
The
.B \-n
option limits the number of refreshes.
Use
.B "top -n 1"
for a one-shot snapshot.
.SH SEE ALSO
free(1), ps(1), uptime(1), vmstat(1)
